{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.A3AntiSelfAdjointLift","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QCharacter"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.gives_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.gives_lift","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L307-L307","doc":"...and drives the even-face correction to the physical lift `κ > 1` (unreachable by the\nself-adjoint branching Schur complement, `A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.amplitude_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.amplitude_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L304-L304","doc":"`E` is nonzero (forced by the strict lift via `amplitude_nonzero`)... ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L302-L302","doc":"**Bar-odd consistency:** the cross-ratio is bar-odd under the involution `σ`\n(`σ E = −E`), matching `DTIndexAmplitudeE.amplitude_barOdd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.amplitude_is_crossRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.amplitude_is_crossRatio","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L299-L299","doc":"**Well-posed frame-free identity:** `E` is the cross-ratio of the connection matrix, the\nunique gauge invariant (`crossRatio_gauge_invariant` + `entry_gauge_movable`), never an\nentry (from `amplitude_injective`; sibling `AmplitudeIsGaugeInvariantCrossRatio`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.infinity_exponent_open","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.infinity_exponent_open","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L294-L294","doc":"The single OPEN datum: a nonzero `∞`-side exponent distinct from the `0`-exponent\n(non-resonant ⇒ genuine theta entries), supplied by the slope-`½` wild construction that\nis not yet built (bean `qou-vkg5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.zero_exponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.zero_exponent","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L290-L290","doc":"The DETERMINED `0`-side Fuchsian exponent: a root of C1's indicial equation\n`c₀² + (q−1)c₀ + (q−1) = 0` (`C1FuchsianExponents`, `C1ZeroSideExponents`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude.mk","kind":"ctor","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L285-L285","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.BirkhoffCrossRatioSuppliesAmplitude","kind":"class","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L266-L307","doc":"**§3b dependent conjecture — the A=3 amplitude `E` is the frame-free, bar-odd cross-ratio\nof the GLOBAL Birkhoff connection matrix, and drives the lift.**\n\n`@conjecture: dependent` (its content depends on the OPEN value of `χ(P)` — the analytic\ntheta closed form of the `0↔∞` cross-ratio, whose `∞`-input is C1's slope-`½` wild\nnormalization; beans `qou-wgnx`, `qou-vkg5`).\n\n**Content-bearing, not self-assuming.**  `zero_exponent` carries the DETERMINED `0`-side\nFuchsian datum (a root of C1's indicial equation — a real INPUT).  `infinity_exponent_open`\nrecords the single missing INPUT (a nonzero `∞`-exponent distinct from `c₀`, non-resonant so\nthe entries are genuine theta amplitudes by `offBlock_multiplier`).  `amplitude_is_crossRatio`\nis the well-posed frame-free identity `E = χ(P)` (from the sibling: `E` frame-free\n(`amplitude_injective`) ⇒ `E` is the unique gauge invariant).  `bar_odd` is the consistency\nclause `σ E = −E` under the bar involution (matching `DTIndexAmplitudeE.amplitude_barOdd`).\n`gives_lift` carries the physical lift as a hypothesis.\n\n**No instance is supplied.**  Deriving `χ(P)`'s value from the analytic construction is the\nopen successor; discharging this by *choosing* `E = χ(P)` to hit `κ`\n(`lift_reachable_by_crossRatio`) is the forbidden fit and is not done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lift_reachable_by_crossRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lift_reachable_by_crossRatio","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L248-L257","doc":"**A derived cross-ratio value reaches the lift only by derivation, never by fit\n(sorry-free).**  `A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_surjective` at the cross-ratio level:\nevery target factor `r` is hit by some cross-ratio value `E = χval`.  Combined with\n`lift_injective_in_crossRatio`, the map `χval ↦ factor` is a bijection — so the lift is\npinned exactly when `χ(P)` is *derived* (bean `qou-wgnx`); *choosing* `χval` to land `r*`\nis the forbidden fit (witness `χval = (factor_sa − r)·A·D·B⁻¹`, anchor-inverted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lift_injective_in_crossRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lift_injective_in_crossRatio","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L234-L246","doc":"**The lift is a well-defined, injective function of the connection cross-ratio\n(sorry-free).**  If the frame-free amplitude is the cross-ratio value, `E = χval`, then the\neven-face lift factor `evenFaceCorrection A (crossTerm B (Csa + E) D)` is determined by\n`χval`; and by `A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_injective` distinct factors force distinct\ncross-ratio values.  So — opposite to a gauge-blind entry — DERIVING `χ(P)` pins the A=3\nlift with no residual ambiguity.  What remains open is the cross-ratio's *value*, not its\nrole.  (This is the corrected bridge: `E = χ(P)`, well-posed, converging with\n`BirkhoffAmplitudeWellPosed`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.distinct_entries_share_crossRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.distinct_entries_share_crossRatio","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L217-L230","doc":"**Distinct bare entries share one cross-ratio (sorry-free).**  Two nonzero entry values\n`e₁, e₂` are realized by diagonal gauges of the *same* base connection, both leaving\n`χ(P) = crossRatio a b c d` unchanged.  A bare entry thus fails to be a well-posed\nfunctional (many entries ↦ one invariant); the frame-free `E` is the invariant, not the\nentry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.entry_gauge_movable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.entry_gauge_movable","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L201-L215","doc":"**A bare entry is gauge-MOVABLE, hence ill-posed as `E` (sorry-free).**  For a base entry\n`b ≠ 0` and ANY nonzero target `e`, a diagonal gauge (here `s = u = v = 1`, `t = e·b⁻¹`)\nsends the entry to `e` while leaving `χ(P)` invariant.  A single entry therefore carries\nno frame-free content: it cannot be the value of the physical scalar `E`.  (Sibling:\n`entry_not_gauge_invariant`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.crossRatio_gauge_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.crossRatio_gauge_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L191-L199","doc":"**`χ(P)` is invariant under the diagonal normalization gauge (sorry-free).**  Rescaling\nthe two bases, `P_{ij} ↦ (d_{∞,i})⁻¹ P_{ij} d_{0,j}` with `d_∞ = (u,v)`, `d_0 = (s,t)`,\nsends `(a,b,c,d)` to `(u⁻¹s·a, u⁻¹t·b, v⁻¹s·c, v⁻¹t·d)`; the four gauge scalars cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.crossRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.crossRatio","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L186-L189","doc":"The frame-free **connection cross-ratio** `χ(P) = P₀₁P₁₀/(P₀₀P₁₁)` (sibling convention;\nreciprocal of `C1ConnectionPoles`'s `P₀₀P₁₁/(P₀₁P₁₀)`), on entries `(a,b,c,d) =\n(P₀₀,P₀₁,P₁₀,P₁₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.offBlock_elliptic_of_resonant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.offBlock_elliptic_of_resonant","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L170-L177","doc":"**Resonance `c₀ = c∞` ⇒ an off-block entry is itself elliptic (sorry-free).**  When the two\nexponents agree the multiplier is `1`, so the entry is σ_q-invariant — `IsQChar.ratio_qInvariant`.\nA generic connection entry is *non-resonant* (`c₀ ≠ c∞`), hence genuinely quasi-periodic;\nonly the balanced cross-ratio, not the entry, is elliptic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.connMultiplier_balance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.connMultiplier_balance","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L162-L168","doc":"**The connection multipliers `c_{ij} = c_{0,j}/c_{∞,i}` satisfy the balance\n`c₀₁·c₁₀ = c₀₀·c₁₁` (sorry-free).**  So `crossRatio_conn_qInvariant` applies to any genuine\nconnection matrix: the ellipticity of `χ(P)` is automatic from the exponent structure, not\nan extra hypothesis.  Both sides equal `c₀₀c₀₁/(c∞₀c∞₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.crossRatio_conn_qInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.crossRatio_conn_qInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L138-L160","doc":"**The CONSTRUCTION lemma — the connection cross-ratio is σ_q-invariant (elliptic) because\nthe exponent multipliers cancel (sorry-free).**  Let the four entries `P₀₀,P₀₁,P₁₀,P₁₁`\nbe q-characters with multipliers `c₀₀,c₀₁,c₁₀,c₁₁`.  For a genuine connection matrix the\nmultipliers are `c_{ij} = c_{0,j}/c_{∞,i}`, which satisfy the **balance**\n`c₀₁·c₁₀ = c₀₀·c₁₁` (both equal `c₀₀c₀₁/(c∞₀c∞₁)`).  Then the cross-ratio\n`χ(P) = P₀₁P₁₀/(P₀₀P₁₁)` is `q`-invariant: its σ_q-multiplier is `(c₀₁c₁₀)/(c₀₀c₁₁) = 1`.\n\nThis *constructs* the frame-free object's ellipticity directly from the q-character\nalgebra — the abstract reason `χ(P)` is theta-valued and `C1ConnectionPoles.connRatio_elliptic`\nholds — and singles out the cross-ratio (not any entry) as the well-posed `E`-carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.offBlock_multiplier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BirkhoffAmplitudeE.offBlock_multiplier","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BirkhoffAmplitudeE.lean#L128-L136","doc":"**An off-block entry's σ_q-multiplier is the exponent ratio `c₀/c∞` (sorry-free).**  If a\n`0`-side component is a q-character (multiplier `c₀`) and an `∞`-side component a\nq-character (multiplier `c∞`), their ratio — the connection off-block model — satisfies\n`h(q·x) = (c₀/c∞)·h(x)` unconditionally in a field.  Amplitude-level content of\n`C1ConnectionPoles.thetaRatio_multiplier` for a ratio of two *different* exponents. ","signatureChunk":0}]}